IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mar-marriage`

-- Marriage Act 1961 (Cth), ss 5, 11-13, 23B, 32, 39, 39F, 41, 42, 42B, 44-46, 48, 50, 89, 113 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_marriage-act-1961.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts: Chloe born 14 March 2003 (c025); Chloe and Liam's notice received 10 April 2029, married in Kings Park
-- 18 May 2029 by a civil celebrant with two witnesses (c053, c054); Jake and Tahlia's notice 10 August 2033, married at the
-- registry 16 September 2033, Ruby born 22 January 2033 (k055, k056); Daniel and Priya's notice 28 October 2024, married by a
-- civil celebrant 30 November 2024 (the cast's date), a Hindu ceremony the week after (d032). Which kind of officer married
-- Jake and Tahlia at the registry is not stated; a s 39(2) officer is ASSUMED.

`Chloe and Liam in Kings Park` MEANS Ceremony WITH
    `the celebrant` IS `a registered marriage celebrant`
    `the place is within the State or area of the authorisation` IS TRUE
    `the celebrant is physically present` IS TRUE
    `a party believed the person was lawfully authorised` IS FALSE
    `the celebrant met each party separately and in person` IS TRUE
    `the s 45 form or a recognised religious form was used` IS TRUE
    `the form showed each party's intention to become a spouse` IS TRUE
    `witnesses over 18` IS 2
    `notice received on` IS 20290410
    `married on` IS 20290518
    `first party's age` IS 26
    `second party's age` IS 29
    `an under-age party has a s 12 order in effect` IS FALSE
    `a party is lawfully married to someone else` IS FALSE
    `the parties are within a prohibited relationship` IS FALSE
    `a party's consent is not a real consent` IS FALSE

